th.com/member/25872-marchenjager","name":"MarchenJager","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T00:46:59-08:00","id":1357321,"title":"","content":"Wow, the Mithras cult write-up is about 1000% better than most. It makes me want to join. Also, it's nice to have a cult that ISN'T nihilism and chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T07:27:36-08:00","id":1357360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357321#post1357321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, the Mithras cult write-up is about 1000% better than most. It makes me want to join. Also, it's nice to have a cult that ISN'T nihilism and chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it heavily referencing Fall of London and if so, does the latter say more about Gwenllian?<br /> <br /> I think examples of a more sympathetic cults would be helpful. So far, I don't want to join any of them, but some of the Dark Ages Roads sound more appealing, even the Road of Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T14:34:28-08:00","id":1357412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1356136#post1356136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that's basically a core of Vampire: The Masquerade, though, that every time you think you're free and clear is another layer of conspiracy. Everyone is a pawn of everyone else back to the Antediluvians. I'm also not of the mind that if you want a group of free Duskborn rebels that it should be the group of vampire ash addicted Google execs.<br /> <br /> What vampires ARE free, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel more like every time you've dug deep enough to start uncovering something, along comes a rainstorm and buries you in a mudslide from all the dirt you've piled up. You think you've figured it all out, then something comes along, yanks the rug out from under you, and you have to start digging to figure out what changed.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1356169#post1356169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ashfinders are.....so damn hokey...doesn't help that Alchemy is just so fucking weird and feels totally out of left field for something vampires do....but it has since the V5 core so theres no getting around it. I just keep getting Made in Chelsea flashbacks with the Ashfinders that makes them impossible to take seriously.<br /> <br /> Some of the IC stuff was very cringe, some was decent to middling, the rest seemed ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see Blood Alchemy as being the evolution of Thin Bloods having access to hedge magic back in time of thin blood. They don't want it just be 'different thaumaturgy' but also more distinctive than hedge magic. But unlike those two it doesn't have alot of established background to draw on and hasn't been given the space the idea deserves to fully develop it. If it's like any other similar concept that gets a rough intiial outline only to be fleshed out later, it might turn out to be alot diffrent than originally envisioned.<br /> <br /> Until then I draw on the aforementioned 'hedge magic' (alchemy and others) as an interim way to flesh it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1356438#post1356438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I'm really impressed with the Church of Caine but stunned that it apparently has no ties with the Sabbat whatsoever. Indeed, seems actively opposed to it. The Lasombra purged the old Cainite Heresy and now they're perfectly willing to do the same thing to the Modern One now that they've joined the Camarilla. The thing is, I'm not sure what the Lasombra issue with the Cainite Heresy is because it's not like most Lasombra BELIEVE in any of the religions they preach. That's the big difference between them and the Ministry after all. The Lasombra love using religion as a tool while the Ministry love it for itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's ties aren't to the modern incarnations of what the Sabbat have become, but something earlier? Or one of its various sub-factions/cults (like the True Black Hand?) Something could have ties or overtones inspired BY the Sabbat (or former Sabbat) without being directly tied to it, methinks. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1356877#post1356877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It may not expressly forbidden anymore - I'm not certain that has been determined. Some of the vampires in the CbN V5 and the Camarilla books discusses Golconda openly, even if they have wrong ideas about it.<br /> <br /> That said, given how much of a catch all the Anarch are, there should be some part of them openly home to Golconda seekers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine they're still trying to figure out what to do with Golconda. There's alot of material to dig through and its going ot take time to piece through/puzzle it all even if they end up discarding most of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 12-28-2019, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T03:24:33-08:00","id":1357497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357412#post1357412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe it's ties aren't to the modern incarnations of what the Sabbat have become, but something earlier? Or one of its various sub-factions/cults (like the True Black Hand?) Something could have ties or overtones inspired BY the Sabbat (or former Sabbat) without being directly tied to it, methinks.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the transcript it does imply that it has links back to the Cainite Heresy, and the Heresy was never connected to the Sabbat, other than the Lasombra's drive to wipe them out. The Sabbat actually contradicts many of the Tenets of the Cainite Heresy.<br /> <br /> For the Sabbat they believe in Noddism only so far as it server their needs, just enough to support their viewpoint of we must wipe out the Antediluvians. The whole Sword of Caine thing always seemed to me to just be convenient rationalisation with scrapes of Noddism. So if the Heresy made a resurgence then breaking from the Sabbat makes sense. There's a scene at the start with someone called Cardinal, the implication I took from the conversation is it was a Sabbat group breaking away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25877-mithras304","name":"Mithras304","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25877_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T03:47:19-08:00","id":1357500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithras304</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357497#post1357497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the transcript it does imply that it has links back to the Cainite Heresy, and the Heresy was never connected to the Sabbat, other than the Lasombra's drive to wipe them out. The Sabbat actually contradicts many of the Tenets of the Cainite Heresy.<br /> <br /> For the Sabbat they believe in Noddism only so far as it server their needs, just enough to support their viewpoint of we must wipe out the Antediluvians. The whole Sword of Caine thing always seemed to me to just be convenient rationalisation with scrapes of Noddism. So if the Heresy made a resurgence then breaking from the Sabbat makes sense. There's a scene at the start with someone called Cardinal, the implication I took from the conversation is it was a Sabbat group breaking away.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually works well with an obscure bit of lore regarding the Path of Caine, which is the fake the Path of Caine is (ironically) a heresy of the Church of Caine. The Path of Caine is just the Path of Blood with the serial numbers filed off. The Assamite Antitribu taught a bastardized version of their religion to the Sabbat because they weren't willing to teach a bunch of non-Banu Haqim their sacred rituals.<br /> <br /> So the Cainite Heresy is the &quot;true&quot; Cainite religion while the Sabbat is their corrupted ISIS version I suppose (or the Path of Blood is and we know even that as taught by the Assamites is the Web of Knives version so it's a double bastardization).<br /> <br /> The one fly in the ointment in all this is Dastur Anosh who is old as shit and still follows the Path of Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T05:05:12-08:00","id":1357510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357500#post1357500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This actually works well with an obscure bit of lore regarding the Path of Caine, which is the fake the Path of Caine is (ironically) a heresy of the Church of Caine. The Path of Caine is just the Path of Blood with the serial numbers filed off. The Assamite Antitribu taught a bastardized version of their religion to the Sabbat because they weren't willing to teach a bunch of non-Banu Haqim their sacred rituals.<br /> <br /> So the Cainite Heresy is the &quot;true&quot; Cainite religion while the Sabbat is their corrupted ISIS version I suppose (or the Path of Blood is and we know even that as taught by the Assamites is the Web of Knives version so it's a double bastardization).<br /> <br /> The one fly in the ointment in all this is Dastur Anosh who is old as shit and still follows the Path of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would subscribe to that view!<br /> <br /> I think the hardest part of trying to present an official cannon is the many contradictory revisions. If there's only one fly in the ointment I'd say we're doing well!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25877-mithras304","name":"Mithras304","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25877_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T05:14:36-08:00","id":1357511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithras304</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357510#post1357510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would subscribe to that view!<br /> <br /> I think the hardest part of trying to present an official cannon is the many contradictory revisions. If there's only one fly in the ointment I'd say we're doing well!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that also reflects life.<br /> <br /> I attend academia and if you want to start a fight then talk about ANYTHING related to history with concrete certainty. History is a pack of lies told by victors, losers, and uninterested observers.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T06:09:20-08:00","id":1357519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357511#post1357511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I attend academia and if you want to start a fight then talk about ANYTHING related to history with concrete certainty. History is a pack of lies told by victors, losers, and uninterested observers.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Truth! In fairness that is probably the best way too look at all the contradictions. They were all 'truths' told by Methuselah's with God Complexes or opportunistic Kindred with an Agenda, the real Truth is probably quite different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25877-mithras304","name":"Mithras304","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25877_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T06:10:13-08:00","id":1357520,"title":"","content":"But... the Setites do want to destroy the world. They're gnostics. They're in that camp of beliefs that says 'The Material world is an illusion an we've been trapped in it by an accident/jealous god and we'd all be better off if we got rid of this illusion and returned to our spiritual one-ness.&quot;<br /> <br /> So do these cults make sense for v20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T06:20:26-08:00","id":1357522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357520#post1357520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... the Setites do want to destroy the world. They're gnostics. They're in that camp of beliefs that says 'The Material world is an illusion an we've been trapped in it by an accident/jealous god and we'd all be better off if we got rid of this illusion and returned to our spiritual one-ness.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They're interested in Set ruling the world and them as gods over it. Shalim is that all reality should be ended, including them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So do these cults make sense for v20? </div> </div> </div>This seems to be a direct sequel to Beckett's Jyhad Diarty more than V5 in general.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T10:42:38-08:00","id":1357564,"title":"","content":"I suppose one could play semantics games about the meaning of 'destroy' - words are vague like that and Set's ilk are just the kind to subscribe to those kind of word games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357500#post1357500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one fly in the ointment in all this is Dastur Anosh who is old as shit and still follows the Path of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know WHY he follows it? Belief that it is the 'correct' way isn't necessarily the only reason. People IRL follow a religion out of habit or a sense of obligation. Or because of self interest/ambition. That's been true historically as well as in modern times.<br /> <br /> And Vampire politics is even more convoluted, nevermind that older vampires tend to have a different (inhuman, if not alien) mindset on top of that. People of roughly the same level of thinking won't always agree on things.<br /> <br /> Edit: And if you want to get even more convoluted you can delve into ideas such as 'was it of his own choice or was he influenced/controlled by others?' Vampires using other vampires as pawns (nevermind other supernaturals) isn't unheard of in WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 12-29-2019, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T11:12:29-08:00","id":1357575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357564#post1357564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we know WHY he follows it? Belief that it is the 'correct' way isn't necessarily the only reason. People IRL follow a religion out of habit or a sense of obligation. Or because of self interest/ambition. That's been true historically as well as in modern times.<br /> <br /> And Vampire politics is even more convoluted, nevermind that older vampires tend to have a different (inhuman, if not alien) mindset on top of that. People of roughly the same level of thinking won't always agree on things.<br /> <br /> Edit: And if you want to get even more convoluted you can delve into ideas such as 'was it of his own choice or was he influenced/controlled by others?' Vampires using other vampires as pawns (nevermind other supernaturals) isn't unheard of in WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, a Path is supposed to replace Humanity in anchoring yourself and preventing succumbing to the beast, a set of morals you live by to avoid losing yourself.<br /> He'd surely have to have a low path rating if he didn't truly believe in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25877-mithras304","name":"Mithras304","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25877_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T11:28:22-08:00","id":1357578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarchenJager</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357213#post1357213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we got a look at a few of the new amalgam Disciplines, what are peoples thoughts? I personally really like Mental Maze, True Love's Face and Slavish Devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like True Love's Face too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T12:14:20-08:00","id":1357585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithras304</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357575#post1357575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While true, a Path is supposed to replace Humanity in anchoring yourself and preventing succumbing to the beast, a set of morals you live by to avoid losing yourself.<br /> He'd surely have to have a low path rating if he didn't truly believe in it?</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of game mechanics I'd agree that explanation won't work. But to be fair I'm largely ignoring those (like I often do for 'narrative' stuff) because game mechanics are abstractions by nature (esp V5), and 'game sheet errors' are a known thing (again Durga Syn). If the setting were 'real' (which I assume for the purposes of suspending disbelief narratively) there's not going to be a rating, is there? And dots on a sheet aren't going to do a great job of simulating the complexities of human philosophy and psychology, nevermind inhuman ones. Ultimately I guess it comes down to which you place more importance in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T12:30:20-08:00","id":1357589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357585#post1357585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of game mechanics I'd agree that explanation won't work. But to be fair I'm largely ignoring those (like I often do for 'narrative' stuff) because game mechanics are abstractions by nature (esp V5), and 'game sheet errors' are a known thing (again Durga Syn). If the setting were 'real' (which I assume for the purposes of suspending disbelief narratively) there's not going to be a rating, is there? And dots on a sheet aren't going to do a great job of simulating the complexities of human philosophy and psychology, nevermind inhuman ones. Ultimately I guess it comes down to which you place more importance in.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, even discounting the mechanics, the Path's are still the means by which Kindred anchor themselves narratively. Without belief in them they would succumb to the beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25877-mithras304","name":"Mithras304","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25877_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T13:31:55-08:00","id":1357596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mithras304</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357589#post1357589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, even discounting the mechanics, the Path's are still the means by which Kindred anchor themselves narratively. Without belief in them they would succumb to the beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but again 'Belief' and interpretation can be pretty complex. Even within a specific belief system. Even if you leave out personal views, how many different branches of Christianity (or sub-branches) can you have, and how do they differ?<br /> <br /> I mean the 'Path of Caine' itself is a prime example. How many different views of 'Caine' are there even if you restrict it to just the VtM Clans (and leave out other editions, etc.) Is the Path of Caine one particular viewpoint of Caine, and if so then what happens when you run up against a different group of vampires who have a different view of what Caine symbolizes/represents from a belief standpoint? And that's just assumine 'true believers' as opposed to people who believe out of habit/indoctrination, or people who 'believe' out of some perceived benefit.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh and the chronological dimension to beliefs. I mean wasn't this what I was arguing about WRT the Sabbat too? Wouldn't the same logic apply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 12-29-2019, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T14:35:11-08:00","id":1357605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357596#post1357596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but again 'Belief' and interpretation can be pretty complex. Even within a specific belief system. Even if you leave out personal views, how many different branches of Christianity (or sub-branches) can you have, and how do they differ?<br /> <br /> I mean the 'Path of Caine' itself is a prime example. How many different views of 'Caine' are there even if you restrict it to just the VtM Clans (and leave out other editions, etc.) Is the Path of Caine one particular viewpoint of Caine, and if so then what happens when you run up against a different group of vampires who have a different view of what Caine symbolizes/represents from a belief standpoint? And that's just assumine 'true believers' as opposed to people who believe out of habit/indoctrination, or people who 'believe' out of some perceived benefit.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh and the chronological dimension to beliefs. I mean wasn't this what I was arguing about WRT the Sabbat too? Wouldn't the same logic apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what your saying, I think there's a distinction between the Path and belief reading into it some more. Paths seem to be more about following certain moral guidelines, so for instance with the Path of Caine one example is &quot;Treating mortals as equals.&quot;. The differences on the finer details about who/what Caine is and did is more linked to ideology relating to things like the Heresy, or the Sabbat's beliefs. In that lens Dastur Anosh can follow the Path of Caine by emulating how he believes Caine to have acted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25877-mithras304","name":"Mithras304","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25877_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T16:55:03-08:00","id":1357637,"title":"","content":"Ultimately a path is the distillation of a faith into a set of core tenets that you could follow. E.g. the 10 commandments of Christianity are fundamental to it, but they are not in and of themselves the entirety of the Christian liturgy.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Sabbat and the Church of Caine, the fundamental difference between the two as far as I can tell is that one is rooted in an inverted Catholocism, whilst the other is thoroughly Gnostic in nature.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat believes that they are the blessed warriors of Caine who shall serve him. He defied God in the form of the Demiurge, and they seek to emulate him and to strike down those who betrayed him, that is to say the 3rd Generation. Things get more complex if you add in the beliefs of the Black Hand as well with the Weeping Stone and the blessings of Zillah.<br /> <br /> The Church of Caine is Gnostic in nature. They believe that the world is, in fact, hell, and all beings are at various stages of enlightenment essentially. Caine brought enlightenment to the world by defying the Demiurge and striking down his brother who was concerned more with physical reality than the spiritual. In turn, he passed that revelation to others through the embrace, hence the church's belief that Cainites are angels.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the two faiths share a common belief in the myth of Caine, the differences arise from everything else. Members of the Sabbat don't think they're angels, typically aren't concerned with God, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T19:35:40-08:00","id":1357660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357500#post1357500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The one fly in the ointment in all this is Dastur Anosh who is old as shit and still follows the Path of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The capacity of people to change their memories to better fit their current setup is pretty impressive. Honestly the idea that he would be old as shit and have accurate memories of the past would be the more insane thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T20:08:04-08:00","id":1357667,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's also noted in Dastur's history that while he developed the Path of Caine, he was actually never quite 100% on the Path of Blood and put in a lot of his own beliefs into it.<br /> <br /> Also, that his loyalty to the Path of Caine, despite being a 9, is actually surprisingly shaky and he has to be incredibly observant because he's fallen off the wagon numerous times during his career.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T03:22:11-08:00","id":1357732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357637#post1357637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Church of Caine is Gnostic in nature. They believe that the world is, in fact, hell, and all beings are at various stages of enlightenment essentially. Caine brought enlightenment to the world by defying the Demiurge and striking down his brother who was concerned more with physical reality than the spiritual. In turn, he passed that revelation to others through the embrace, hence the church's belief that Cainites are angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Camarilla guide says that they believe Caine opposes the Demiurge, <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> says that they believe he's his representative.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T04:22:06-08:00","id":1357737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357637#post1357637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately a path is the distillation of a faith into a set of core tenets that you could follow. E.g. the 10 commandments of Christianity are fundamental to it, but they are not in and of themselves the entirety of the Christian liturgy.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Sabbat and the Church of Caine, the fundamental difference between the two as far as I can tell is that one is rooted in an inverted Catholocism, whilst the other is thoroughly Gnostic in nature.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat believes that they are the blessed warriors of Caine who shall serve him. He defied God in the form of the Demiurge, and they seek to emulate him and to strike down those who betrayed him, that is to say the 3rd Generation. Things get more complex if you add in the beliefs of the Black Hand as well with the Weeping Stone and the blessings of Zillah.<br /> <br /> The Church of Caine is Gnostic in nature. They believe that the world is, in fact, hell, and all beings are at various stages of enlightenment essentially. Caine brought enlightenment to the world by defying the Demiurge and striking down his brother who was concerned more with physical reality than the spiritual. In turn, he passed that revelation to others through the embrace, hence the church's belief that Cainites are angels.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the two faiths share a common belief in the myth of Caine, the differences arise from everything else. Members of the Sabbat don't think they're angels, typically aren't concerned with God, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a much more eloquent way of putting it, yes this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25877-mithras304","name":"Mithras304","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25877_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T17:22:20-08:00","id":1357906,"title":"","content":"I love the fact the Cult of Helena is completely unrelated to Helena. I'm also of the mind that Francois Villon is probably the guy behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T17:36:28-08:00","id":1357914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357732#post1357732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the Camarilla guide says that they believe Caine opposes the Demiurge, <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> says that they believe he's his representative.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd probably side with cults over the Camarilla book, but I think the position is a nuanced one. Caine did defy the Demiurge, but that defiance wasn't looked down upon, it was rewarded. The same way a father might respect a son that can stand up for himself, even if he thinks the son is foolish.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357906#post1357906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the fact the Cult of Helena is completely unrelated to Helena. I'm also of the mind that Francois Villon is probably the guy behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have we actually heard anything about Villon other than him going to ground to escape the SI? I mean I could see him having a distant hand but this sounds like something American Kindred are running and I don't think Villon would dare risk Helena's displeasure... after all, everyone who's anyone knows where he lives.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T15:42:45-08:00","id":1358094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1356049-spoilers-cults-of-the-blood-gods-discussion?p=1357906#post1357906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the fact the Cult of Helena is completely unrelated to Helena. I'm also of the mind that Francois Villon is probably the guy behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25872-marchenjager","name":"MarchenJager","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:57:50-08:00","id":1358325,"title":"","content":"At $122,000 in funding - FORBIDDEN FAITHS PDF \u2014 RUINOUS BELIEFS: Help us fund a chapter dedicated to cults that believe vampires are tools of the devil, demons, and evil spirits. These are not mustache-twirling villains, but Kindred who firmly believe their role is as hell's emissaries.<br /> &quot;I don't know what you heard about me,but a saint cant get a dollar outta me. No horns ,no fork you can't see I'm a motherfucking I-N-F-E-R-N-A-L-I-S-T&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T19:19:50-08:00","id":1358328,"title":"","content":"So, Path of Night? And Cathari?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_l